    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48874" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trans-rhēnānus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that is beyond the Rhine</i>, <i>Transrhenish</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Germani,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 5, 2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hostes,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the Batavians</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 1, 2, § 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lares,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 20, 4, 4</span></i>
			. — As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Transrhēnāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>those living beyond the Rhine</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				4, 16</span></i>.</div>
